# EAS Hosting deploy manifest — overrides .gitignore for `eas deploy`.
#
# Without this, eas deploy inherits .gitignore (which ignores dist/, node_modules/, .expo/) and skips the
# exported /_expo/ (JS) and /assets/ (images) folders, so the live site 404s all static assets — the
# Welcome logo + onboarding slate backgrounds + favicon all vanished. An (almost) empty .easignore means
# "upload the whole dist as exported." We only exclude the vestigial node_modules assets copied into the
# export, which aren't referenced by the web bundle.
dist/assets/node_modules/
